1
00:00:00,301 --> 00:00:06,013
This is Eva. An Arch Linux distro with a desktop of its
own.

2
00:00:06,763 --> 00:00:10,987
Press Super to find your apps and files in one place.

3
00:00:11,737 --> 00:00:16,249
Prisma keeps your files close, with previews and tabs.

4
00:00:16,999 --> 00:00:20,791
Super B brings your open apps together.

5
00:00:21,541 --> 00:00:25,357
With Tab, you can see your windows and change workspaces.

6
00:00:26,107 --> 00:00:29,996
Choose a layout and give each window its place.

7
00:00:30,746 --> 00:00:37,754
Here is the game library. Browse the covers with your
mouse or the arrow keys.

8
00:00:38,504 --> 00:00:42,776
Pick a different background for each screen or workspace.

9
00:00:43,526 --> 00:00:48,902
Prefer something that moves? You can use a video as your
wallpaper.

10
00:00:49,652 --> 00:00:53,372
Add a clock or leave yourself a note on the desktop.

11
00:00:54,122 --> 00:00:57,698
Light or dark, with the colors you like.

12
00:00:58,448 --> 00:01:02,624
Drag the bar modules into place and make room for what you
use.

13
00:01:03,375 --> 00:01:08,583
Your keyboard layout and shortcuts are here, ready to
change.

14
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:13,029
Keep your events and reminders together in the calendar.

15
00:01:13,779 --> 00:01:17,163
Take a look at how your computer is running.

16
00:01:17,913 --> 00:01:21,417
Control your music and video from the desktop.

17
00:01:22,167 --> 00:01:27,615
There is room for a little company, too. Meet the desktop
pets.

18
00:01:28,365 --> 00:01:32,733
Connect your AI provider and keep the chat within reach.

19
00:01:33,484 --> 00:01:37,660
You can even choose how Eva looks when your computer
starts.

20
00:01:38,410 --> 00:01:42,826
That is Eva. Download the beta and take a look around.
